BOTW x Minecraft bridge: the native side (implementation/botw-live-bridge)

This folder contains work adapted from, or learnt from, the projects below. Their licence texts are kept beside this
file. No file of the game, of Cemu or of Minecraft is redistributed here.


SkyCraft, by chasmlol (MIT; LICENSE-SkyCraft)
https://github.com/chasmlol/SkyCraft, revision bfcaf178524b92c2cdeb88e4ce0f13ef9ded6f32

  live.h             the shared memory's ownership, guarded values and rings, adapted from skse/src/Link.cpp
  native_geometry.h  triangle/box tests, plane-guided filling of blocks and the coarsening of steep surfaces,
                     adapted from Collision.cpp
  finite_patch.py    the same block filling, for the offline check
  render.h, integrate.h, live_scene.h
                     the meaning of the render ring's records and the alpha, tint and light rules, after
                     WorldRender.cpp
  The protocol header (../botwcraft-fabric/protocol/botwcraft_protocol.h) is SkyCraft's skycraft_protocol.h with
  its names changed and fields added; it is included directly.
  The Minecraft mod in ../botwcraft-fabric (BotwCraft) is an adapted, renamed copy of SkyCraft's mod; see its
  own LICENSE, which is SkyCraft's.


BetterVR, by Crementif (MIT; LICENSE-BetterVR)
https://github.com/Crementif/BotW-BetterVR, revision 2e06b31f062408d3293a392df418da0ab37b1f23

  vendor/vkroots.h   copied unchanged from dependencies/vkroots.h (see vkroots below)
  pack/patch_bridge.asm, probe.cpp, body.h, physical.h
                     the patch sequences for the 3D frame buffer marker, the camera and projection, the gamepad
                     read and the player's character controller, adapted from
                     patch_RND_Find3DFrameBuffer.asm, patch_RND_StereoRendering_CameraAndProjection.asm,
                     patch_CTRL_ButtonInput.asm, patch_CTRL_EntityController.asm,
                     src/hooking/framebuffer.cpp, camera.cpp, layer.cpp, entity_controller.cpp
  player_render.h, link_bones.h, actors.h, runes.h
                     places and layouts first found in patch_FirstPersonMode.asm, patch_CTRL_Bones.asm,
                     skeleton.cpp, game_state.cpp, cemu_hooks.h and include/game_structs.h; each was checked
                     against the running US v208 program before use
  No VR code (OpenXR, stereo projection, shared D3D runtime) is taken.


vkroots (Apache-2.0 OR MIT; LICENSE-vkroots-Apache-2.0)
  vendor/vkroots.h, the Vulkan layer framework, unchanged.


Vulkan-Headers, by The Khronos Group (Apache-2.0 OR MIT)
https://github.com/KhronosGroup/Vulkan-Headers, v1.4.328, revision 9a0f3099c8a9607a7c0f3127d8abfdc19a93e8c5

  Needed to compile only. Not in this repository: docs/building.md says how to fetch it.


WiiXLaunch-BotW, by Bladesaw Studios (GPL v3; LICENSE-WiiXLaunch, kept for reference)
https://github.com/BladesawStudios/wiixlaunch-botw, revision 1bdab2d1978efb2bab1d296b7d2a8c408b94aa0a

  Studied for how the player is found, the layout of an actor and the game's physics synchronisation
  (include/wiixlaunch/botw/game/player.hpp, actor.hpp, docs/actor-transforms.md).
  No code of it is copied into this project.


The Breath of the Wild decompilation (zeldaret/botw)
https://github.com/zeldaret/botw

  Read for the names and the meaning of the game's classes and data. It describes another build of the game; no
  code of it is copied.


Cemu (MPL 2.0)
https://github.com/cemu-project/Cemu, v2.6

  The bridge calls functions Cemu exports (osLib_registerHLEFunction, memory_getBase, gameMeta_getTitleId) and
  follows the register layout of its PPCState.h. No code of Cemu is copied; Cemu itself is not included.


The game

  The bridge is made for The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild, Wii U, US version, update v208. It holds
  addresses and offsets of that program, names of its actors and bones, and patches written for it. It holds no
  part of the program itself and none of the game's assets. A copy of the game the player owns is needed to play.

